course: dictionary
lesson: 9802
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word swab is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: A swab can be a small piece of cotton wool on a stick, used to clean a wound. It can also be a sample taken from your nose or throat so it can be tested for germs. Ask yourself: is someone cleaning something, or taking a sample for a test?
explain: To swab can also be a doing word. «To swab the deck» means to clean a ship's floor with a mop. When swab is a thing, it is a noun. When it is an action, it is a verb.
fact: A swab is a small piece of cotton wool, often on a stick.
fact: Nurses and doctors use swabs to clean a wound or put on medicine.
fact: A swab can also be a sample taken from the nose, throat or mouth, so it can be tested for germs.
fact: «The swab only goes a little way in.» This is from a text about a test, so the swab is the sample, not the cotton wool.
fact: «To swab the deck» means to clean a ship's floor with a mop.
exercise: «The nurse put cream on the cut with a clean swab.» What is a swab here? | A type of sea bird | A large bar of soap | *A small piece of cotton wool on a stick | A tiny pirate ship
exercise: «The nurse took a swab from his throat, so the lab could test for germs.» What is the swab? | A kind of bandage | *A sample taken for testing | A loud cough | A mop for cleaning a ship's deck
exercise: Sailors «swab the deck» every morning. What does swab mean in this phrase? | To paint the sails | *To clean the floor with a mop | To count the coins | To cook breakfast
test: «She had a throat swab at the clinic.» What is a swab here? | A type of sweet | A ship's mop | *A sample taken from the throat to test for germs | A loud cough
test: «The pirates had to swab the deck before dinner.» What does swab mean? | *To clean with a mop | To count the coins | To cook dinner | To paint the sails
exam: Which sentence uses swab as a verb, a doing word? | The swab was white and fluffy | The nurse held a swab in her hand | The lab put the swab in a box | *The crew had to swab the deck every morning
